    Wire the frozen rstd table lookup into the hidden norm chain
    
    The norm first and second stages now commit, absorb and prove the frozen-table
    lookup over the rounding rows: key column zero reads the committed index value
    slot and column one the committed table value slot, the multiplicity bits and
    mask go through the existing sample and tree machinery, the lookup challenge is
    drawn after the plan, table identity and message roots, and the lookup claims
    and rows join the hidden BAT, fold, mask budget and retained trees.
    
    The verifier binds the trusted table configuration (identity, content root,
    real length, encoding, version) from the plan and checks that the table object
    it reads hashes to the trusted content root; the table view check also compares
    the public first-row padding pair. The rounding plan's trusted table length
    keeps every committed index below the real length through the index-bound
    relation. The hidden fixture builds a synthetic ranged table and commits
    matching index and value slots.
    
    The positive chain plus nine negatives pass: committed value, committed index,
    out-of-range index, table identity, table content, table length, padded row,
    key-side padding, and tampered message roots and claims. Hard gate unchanged.
    
    partial progress

